  (fn-do _ call-builder Typed
    (param site SyntaxId)
    (param source Operand)
    (param builder TypeId)
    (param item (? Operand) (= null))
    ; A call of what a value of a function type that takes nothing, or the one `item`, holds, given the
    ; data it holds: the function that builds a slot, as a slot outlet calls it. What runs is not known
    ; here, so the call is checked for a panic, which the type pass has said of the caller. A type that
    ; carries errors answers with its value or one of them, and an error leaves the function at the
    ; call, as the type pass kept.
